Day 4: Salesforce Flow Builder & Automation


1. What is Flow Builder?
Flow Builder is a powerful, point-and-click tool in Salesforce used to automate complex business processes without writing code. 
It allows users to create logic that can perform actions like updating records, sending emails, and guiding users through multi-step screens.
By using a visual interface, businesses can streamline their workflows and ensure data consistency across the enterprise.
===========================================================================================================================================================================================================================
 2. Types of Flows
Understanding which flow to use depends on how the automation should be triggered.  
\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\
Screen Flow: A flow that requires user interaction. 
It guides users through a specific business process by providing screens where they can input or view data.  

Record-Triggered Flow: An automated process that launches in the background whenever a record is created, updated, or deleted.
It is ideal for "behind-the-scenes" updates that don't require user input.
===========================================================================================================================================================================================================================
3. Automation Ideas (College Management System)Automation helps reduce manual workload and improves accuracy within a campus environment.
Here are five suggested processes:
Auto Email After Registration: Send a welcome packet and login credentials immediately after a student record is created. 
Automatic Student ID Generation: Use a flow to format and assign a unique institutional ID number as soon as a student enrolls. 
Course Capacity Notifications: Automatically alert faculty members via email or Slack when a course reaches its maximum student limit.
Fee Deadline Reminders: Schedule automated reminders to be sent to students 7 days before their tuition payment is due.
Dynamic Seat Updates: Automatically decrease the Remaining Seats field on a Course record every time a new Enrollment record is finalized.  
===========================================================================================================================================================================================================================
4. Flow Diagram: Auto Student ID Generation
Flow Logic Components

#The Trigger (Start Node):  
Type: Record-Triggered Flow.  
Object: Student (Student__c).
Condition: Executes only when a record is created.  
Timing: Runs "After the record is saved" to ensure the ID is applied to a permanent record.
#Get Records (Data Collection):  
The flow searches for the Department object related to the student.  
It fetches the Department_Code__c (e.g., "AI&DS" or "CSE") to include in the ID.
#Decision Point (Branching Logic):  Check Admission Type: The flow asks, "Is this a Regular or Lateral Entry student?
"Regular Path: Uses the standard starting sequence (e.g., 2026-).
Lateral Path: Appends a specific identifier (e.g., 2026-LE-) to distinguish their academic track.
#The Formula Variable (The ID Generator):  
A formula resource inside Flow Builder creates the final string.  
Structure: YEAR(TODAY()) + Dept_Code__c + Random_or_Sequential_Number.
Result: Converts raw data into a unique identifier like 2026-AIDS-055.
#Final Action 
(Update Record):  The flow writes the generated string into the Student_ID_Field__c.
  Notification: Optionally triggers an automated email to the student with their new ID. 
===========================================================================================================================================================================================================================
5. Manual vs. Automated Process
Workflow:
Faculty write names on paper and manually type them into Excel later. 
Students scan a QR code; Salesforce immediately updates their attendance record.
Problems:
High risk of data entry errors, lost paperwork, and delayed reporting. 
Data is captured in real-time with 100% accuracy and instant visibility. 
